        "answer": {
          "short": "Histogram bars have width $1$ and heights $3,6,4,2$, centred at $x=2,3,4,5$. The polygon joins $(1,0),(2,3),(3,6),(4,4),(5,2),(6,0)$.",
          "worked": "Draw adjoining bars over $[1.5,2.5]$, $[2.5,3.5]$, $[3.5,4.5]$ and $[4.5,5.5]$, with heights $3$, $6$, $4$ and $2$. Join the centres of their top edges, extending the polygon to $(1,0)$ and $(6,0)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": [
            {
              "id": "cont-hist-polygon-graph",
              "role": "solution",
              "format": "tikz",
              "code": "% mathsmap-diagram-colours {\"version\":1,\"kind\":\"graph\",\"base\":[],\"semantic\":[{\"name\":\"seriesBlue\",\"hex\":\"268CFF\",\"reason\":\"frequency histogram and polygon\"},{\"name\":\"areaBlue\",\"hex\":\"D4E8FF\",\"reason\":\"histogram rectangles whose total area is assessed\"}],\"reference\":\"cont-hist-polygon-graph\"}\n\\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1.1cm,y=0.75cm]\n\\definecolor{seriesBlue}{HTML}{268CFF}\n\\definecolor{areaBlue}{HTML}{D4E8FF}\n\\special{dvisvgm:raw <metadata data-graph-strokes=\"1\"/>}\n\\path[use as bounding box] (-0.5,-0.55) rectangle (6.7,6.65);\n\\foreach \\l/\\r/\\h in {1.5/2.5/3,2.5/3.5/6,3.5/4.5/4,4.5/5.5/2}{\\draw[draw=seriesBlue,fill=areaBlue,line width=0.8pt] (\\l,0) rectangle (\\r,\\h);}\n\\draw[line width=0.5pt] (0,0)--(6.5,0) node[right] {$x$};\n\\draw[line width=0.5pt] (0,0)--(0,6.5) node[right] {$y$};\n\\foreach \\v in {1,2,3,4,5,6}{\\draw[line width=0.4pt] (\\v,-0.07)--(\\v,0.07);\\node[below] at (\\v,-0.09) {\\special{dvisvgm:raw <g data-graph-text=\"tick\">}$\\v$\\special{dvisvgm:raw </g>}};}\n\\foreach \\v in {1,2,3,4,5,6}{\\draw[line width=0.4pt] (-0.07,\\v)--(0.07,\\v);\\node[left] at (-0.09,\\v) {\\special{dvisvgm:raw <g data-graph-text=\"tick\">}$\\v$\\special{dvisvgm:raw </g>}};}\n\\draw[seriesBlue,line width=0.8pt] (1,0)--(2,3)--(3,6)--(4,4)--(5,2)--(6,0);\n\\end{tikzpicture}",
              "src": null,
              "widthMm": 70,
              "alt": "Mathematical diagram",
              "overlayOf": null,
              "transparent": false,
